designs.library_api:
Import rules: `inazuma.nucleo.*` has zero imports from juegos/servicio/cli. `inazuma.juegos.<x>` imports only nucleo, and the relationship is enforced by a test (import-linter-style AST check). Games never import each other. ie2.comun/ie3.comun are only visible to their own versions.
Stable nucleo facade:
- contenedores.fa.open(path) -> FaArchive(.entries, .read(p), .replace(p, bytes), .write(out))
- compresion.{lz10, blz, sszl}.{decompress, compress}
- graficos.ctpk.{decode->PIL.Image, encode}
- graficos.qna.regions()
- graficos.atlas_paint.paint(atlas, rects, items)
- graficos.pac_sprite.{decode, encode}
- fuentes.bcfnt.{parse, patch_glyphs}
- fuentes.nftr.metrics
- texto.fullwidth.encode_fullwidth
- texto.wrap.layout(text, advances, profile)
- eventos.pkb.{read_index, iter_events, pack}
- eventos.ssd.{parse, replace}
- ejecutable.cro.{literals, relocate_string}
- ejecutable.smdh.set_title
- media.moflex.{from_mods, to_mp4, from_mp4}
- media.sadl.{to_wav, from_wav}
- construir.candidata.Candidate
- validar.bloqueo_dialogo.validate
Pure functions work on bytes and Paths, with no module-level side effects and no hardcoded paths (everything comes from config.Paths).

designs.tests_plan:
Four tiers.
(1) Unit: the moved tools/test_*.py plus new round-trip tests per nucleo format on synthetic data: lz10, sszl, ARCV children, CTPK encode/decode, PAC, SSD, PackNum, SMDH, subtitle dat<->SRT. No ROM data in the repo.
(2) Compat, runs without ROMs:
- a shim import matrix, where every old tools name imports from a clean interpreter with cwd=root and with cwd=elsewhere where it worked before;
- a surface snapshot (dir() and signatures captured at stage 0);
- identity tests (ie1.dialogo.layout is build_ie1_probe.layout; nucleo.texto.fullwidth.encode_fullwidth is dialogue_typography.encode_fullwidth);
- a lock test (dialogue_lock.validate plus the raw sha of the 4 locked files equal to the baseline);
- the import-linter contracts (games->nucleo only, no cross-game imports);
- an AST check that the shims contain no logic.
(3) Layer smoke, local: a script enumerates work/**/apply.py, prepare.py and validate.py and runs each in a subprocess with cwd=root under `python -X importtime -c` import-only mode where possible, or with `--dry-run` flags where layers support it. It compares against a stage-0 baseline of pass/fail. Any new failure blocks the stage.
(4) Golden rebuild, local, ROM required: rebuild candidates v65/v66 from their bases through the old layer scripts and through `ie123 build`. Compare the sha256 of every output file, the CRO and the final xdelta against tests/golden. The comparison must be byte-identical. Offline tests are not the end of the gate: per PROTOCOLO_QA_IE1, a stage touching build/install code also needs an emulator run up to the first pachanga with several NPCs before it counts as stable.
Service contract tests: every GameActions implementation passes a shared parametrized suite (list_assets JSON-serializable, dry_run import returns Issues without writing, progress callback monotonic, cancel honored).
